<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate falls in auction.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand rose, Banco de Mexico said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	29.08	    -77	     28.92     29.25</p>
<p>91-Day	27.70	    -176	    25.38     28.24</p>
<p>182-Day     27.09	    -70	     26.95     27.17</p>
<p>343-Day     26.50				26.39     26.60</p>
<p>Last week the 350-day paper was assigned at 26.74 pct.  </p>
<p>    Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.60 bln pesos	    2.89</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   5.87 bln pesos	    6.52</p>
<p>182-Day     900 million pesos   4.89 bln pesos	    5.43</p>
<p>343-Day     600 million pesos   2.16 bln pesos	    3.60</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 4.7 this week compared with 4.29 the week before, on demand of 14.15 billion pesos.</p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			   17 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   54 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			   8 basis points</p>
<p>    343-Day			  10 basis points</p>
<p>-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9559.</p>
</text>
